/-! # Weights of a rational module generated by a Borel eigenvector

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Proposition 22.17, p.467, its multiplicity-one
and weight-bound assertions in finite dimension; Proposition 22.14, p.466.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-primitive-cyclic-weight-bound)

Weight subspaces are equalizers of the restricted coaction and the character
coaction. Evaluating at the universal point proves that this is precisely the
identity over every coefficient algebra, including nonreduced algebras. The same
interpretation applies to the Borel eigenvector hypothesis. Characters are actual
group-scheme morphisms, written additively for the root datum and the final sum.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory
open scoped TensorProduct MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RationalHighestWeight

/-- A cyclic rational module generated by a nonzero Borel eigenvector has exactly
that line as its generating weight space; all its weights are the generating
weight minus a nonnegative integral sum of the specified simple roots.
Source: Milne, Proposition 22.17, p.467, and Proposition 22.14, p.466.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-primitive-cyclic-weight-bound)

Proof plan, following all six steps of the node:
1. Write c(v) as a finite sum d_j tensor f_j with independent f_j. Coassociativity,
   contracted by the dual coefficient functionals, makes the span D of the d_j
   stable. The counit puts v in D, and cyclicity gives D=M.
2. By lem-sfb-bruhat-longest-cell-charts, choose the root-reversing involution w0
   and representative n0. Since n0 squared lies in T, translation by n0 takes
   U n0 B to Uminus B, a dense open affine chart. The same node gives reducedness
   of G. By lem-sfb-borel-root-product-coordinates and
   lem-sfb-reductive-root-subgroup-parametrizations, ordered opposite root groups
   identify Uminus with affine r-space, with conjugation characters beta_i negative.
3. Expand their orbit of v as the finite polynomial sum z^I m_I. Its constant
   coefficient is v. Compare coefficients in t f(z)=lambda(t) f(beta_i(t)z_i)
   over arbitrary coefficient algebras: m_I has weight lambda+sum I_i beta_i.
   This is the argument of Milne 22.14 and uses no division by factorials.
4. Let C span the m_I. The orbit of v modulo C vanishes on the affine chart
   Uminus B, since B acts by the given character. Apply
   lemma-nagata-reduced-dense-image-schematic to its dense open immersion into
   reduced G. By def-nagata-scheme-theoretic-image the kernel of restriction of
   regular functions is zero (the immersion is quasi-compact). Thus the quotient
   orbit vanishes on G, so all coefficients d_j lie in C. Step 1 gives M=C.
5. Express each negative beta_i as minus a nonnegative sum of simple roots using
   lem-sfb-reductive-borel-pair-structure. Independence of the simple roots makes
   that sum nonzero for I nonzero. Hence only m_0=v has weight lambda.
6. Extract a weight-vector basis from the coefficients, retaining v. Comparing
   its coordinates at the universal torus point shows that a nonzero mu-weight
   vector has a basis component with character mu. Step 5 gives its simple-root
   bound; for mu=lambda only the component v is possible. The reverse inclusion
   of Fv is the eigenvector hypothesis. For no roots, the sole monomial is 1,
   so cyclicity gives M=Fv. Neither simplicity nor characteristic zero is used. -/
theorem primitive_cyclic_weight_bound
    {F : Type u} [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F]
    (G T B U : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F))))
    [IsAffine G.X.left] [IsAffine T.X.left] [IsAffine B.X.left]
    (hG : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsReductive G)
    (iT : T ⟶ G) (hT : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsMaximalTorus iT)
    (hsplit : ∃ r : ℕ, Nonempty (T ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus F r))
    (iB : B ⟶ G) (hB : IsBorelGroupScheme iB.hom.hom)
    (j : T ⟶ B) (hj : j ≫ iB = iT)
    (iU : U ⟶ B) (p : B ⟶ T)
    (hUclosed : IsClosedSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom)
    (hUnormal : IsNormalSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom)
    (hUsmooth : Smooth U.X.hom) (hUconn : ConnectedSpace U.X.left)
    (hUunip : SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent U)
    (hUmax : ∀ (N : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iN : N ⟶ B),
      IsClosedSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom → IsNormalSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom →
      Smooth N.X.hom → ConnectedSpace N.X.left → SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent N →
      ∃ f : N ⟶ U, f ≫ iU = iN)
    (hp : j ≫ p = 𝟙 T)
    (hker : IsPullback iU.hom.hom (toUnit U.X) p.hom.hom η[T.X])
    (hsplitB : IsIso ((fst U.X T.X ≫ iU.hom.hom) * (snd U.X T.X ≫ j.hom.hom)))
    [IsCommMonObj T.X] [IsCommMonObj (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)]
    (aG : ModObj T.X G.X) (aB : ModObj T.X B.X)
    (haG : aG.smul = (iT.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 G.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj G.X)
    (haB : aB.smul = (j.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 B.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj B.X)
    (Φ : Finset (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))))
    (P : RootDatum Φ
      (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)))
    (base : P.Base) (hred : P.IsReduced)
    (hroot : ∀ α : Φ, P.root α = α.val)
    (hpair : ∀ (χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (ν : Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)),
      ν.toMul.hom.hom ≫ χ.toMul.hom.hom =
        (𝟙 (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)) ^ (P.toLinearMap χ ν))
    (hΦ : ∀ χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)),
      χ ∈ Φ ↔ χ ≠ 0 ∧ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T G aG χ.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    (hpos : ∀ α : Φ,
      base.IsPos α ↔ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T B aB α.val.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module F M] [FiniteDimensional F M]
    (c : M →ₗ[F] M ⊗[F] coordinateAlgebra G)
    (hcoassoc : HopfAction.Coassociative F (coordinateAlgebra G) M c)
    (hcounit : HopfAction.Counital F (coordinateAlgebra G) M c)
    (lam : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
    (v : M) (hv : v ≠ 0)
    (heigen : (coordinateMap iB).toLinearMap.lTensor M (c v) =
      v ⊗ₜ[F] characterElement (p ≫ lam.toMul))
    (hcyclic : ∀ N : Submodule F M, IsStable c N → v ∈ N → N = ⊤) :
    LinearMap.eqLocus ((coordinateMap iT).toLinearMap.lTensor M ∘ₗ c)
        ((TensorProduct.mk F M (coordinateAlgebra T)).flip (characterElement lam.toMul)) =
      Submodule.span F {v} ∧
    ∀ mu : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)),
      LinearMap.eqLocus ((coordinateMap iT).toLinearMap.lTensor M ∘ₗ c)
        ((TensorProduct.mk F M (coordinateAlgebra T)).flip (characterElement mu.toMul)) ≠ ⊥ →
      ∃ n : Φ → ℕ, mu = lam - ∑ α ∈ base.support, n α • P.root α := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.RationalHighestWeight
